# 04 Assets and the library

Everything about *content Cyrus can use or ship*: legal rules, the catalog, ingestion, the owner's sound library, the Minecraft reference policy, motion/effect assets, the library backend, and takedown/filters. Staging data is **not in git, not served, not in the database**; it lives on disk (`/tank/cyrus-library-staging`).

## Legal ledger and asset classes (`lib/cyrus/assets3d/ledger.ts`, client-safe copy used by server and studios)
| Class | Meaning | Store beyond job | Add to library | Redistribute | Deliverable |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `user-original` | authored by the user in a studio | yes | yes | yes | full |
| `ai-generated-for-user` | made by Cyrus for the user | yes | yes | yes | full |
| `platform-library` | Nxeon-owned or CC0 only | yes | yes | yes | full |
| `third-party-licensed` | uploaded/imported under someone else's licence | yes | **no** | no | full |
| `game-derived` | derived from a game's own files | **no** | **no** | **no** | delta-only |

The rule: **game-derived content never outlives its job, never enters a library, never ships.** `libraryEligible()` allows automatic contribution only for content authored inside Cyrus (provenance source `user`/`ai`/`library`) with an empty `derivedFrom`; uploads, imports, templates and anything derived from other bytes are never eligible. Eligible is not published: content filters and the Terms grant still gate publication. Every manifest carries provenance (`source`, `derivedFrom`) and a legal

## Licence rules (owner decisions)
- **CC0 only** in the community library; **no creator credit** (CC-BY excluded, so there is no attribution burden); "usable by anyone" semantics for contributed assets are an open decision (does it include "Use in project").
- Every upstream source was checked on its own page; an aggregator's blanket "CC0" was not relied on. Per-source/pack quotes and exclusions are in `LICENCE-LEDGER.csv` (about 670 rows) and `_lic/` in staging.
- Excluded and kept aside: 4,132 CC-BY rows; the Quaternius Bestiary (new no-redistribution licence); Mixamo/CMU (terms); 88 PVFX Foundry rows (CC0 only by description text); CC-BY-NC and Sampling+ FSD50K clips. Rejected or unreadable sources (Freesound direct, BigSoundBank, OpenGameArt bulk, NASA 3D, ShareTextures/Texturecan/Poly Pizza) are listed in the ledger with quotes.
- Sound audio is **never in git and never served raw**; the proprietary library is served only when cleared.

## Staging layout and ingestion (r-J, `/tank/cyrus-library-staging`)
`kenney/ quaternius/ kaykit/ polyhaven/ ambientcg/ khronos/ smithsonian/ thebasemesh/ game-icons/ sound/ motion/` hold source packs; `catalog.jsonl` and the `catalog-*.jsonl` family hold per-asset rows (publishable, excluded-ccby, excluded-pending-licence, proprietary-sfx, motion2-publishable); `catalog-v2/` holds the enriched entries (`entries3-staged-cc0.jsonl` = 62,777 entries, CC0 + owner proprietary, 56.5% fully described, 62,444 published / 43 held / 290 removed; flags 422 trademark, 87 vi

Staged now (CC0): about 62k rows: 10,278 models, 2,946 PBR sets, 1,430 HDRIs, 38,464 Kenney sprites (inflated), 2,752 textures, 127 decals, about 6,000 sounds including the owner's 2,964-file proprietary library. Open: Smithsonian 199 of 2,326 verified models staged; FSD50K download slow (keep the CC0 half only); NASA models and Warfork sounds need the owner's call; 10 sounds failed to decode; thumbnails for about 18k assets before any AI tagging; numeric pack folder names (1-10) carry no descri

## Catalog v2
Each asset has a content-hash id `cat:<sha256>`, kind (model, PBR set, texture, sprite, HDRI, decal, sound, music, plus motion/effect kinds: flipbook, particle-texture, animation-clip, animated-model, motion-preset, effect-preset), title, description (<=140), controlled tags + up to 8 free tags, one primary and up to 3 secondary categories, measured descriptors (audio duration/intensity/pitch band/loopable/channels; texture size/palette/transparency/tileable/style), game fit, licence tier and pr

## Library backend (r26)
Content-addressed object store (local or S3, caps, 30-day retention), lazy deterministic derivatives (thumb, preview-ogg, glb-opt, bundle), signed 5-minute viewer-scoped URLs (raw audio never; proprietary only when cleared), **automatic contribution** with strict filters and a hold queue, exact/near dedupe (image dhash, audio envelope, glb facts, motion JSON), reports and **takedown** (a legal report or 3 reporters holds; takedown removes now, purges derivatives, marks dependents; **dependent mo

## Takedown, filters, moderation (r32, r40)
Content filters: trademark list (a stub until the owner supplies one; editable in admin), real-weapon names (hold vs flag is an open decision), violence/extremist/drugs/adult, text-only today (no NFKC/confusables or pixel/audio classifier: open item O-8). r32 fixed: one account could mass-hold assets with copyright reports (now 5 auto-holds per reporter per 24 h) and takedown now also holds stored near-copies. Admin (`/admin/cyrus/library/*`): hold-queue decisions, near-duplicates, contribution 

## The owner's proprietary SFX library
514 MP3s first (board upload), later 2,964 files in `/tank/cyrus-library-incoming` (zip CRC-verified, unzipped under staging `sound/nxeon-proprietary`). Licence (per the bundle's own PDF): licensor Excelerator.tech, non-transferable; **modifying and using in games is allowed; distributing or making the files available alone or in a bundle is prohibited**. Therefore: customers hear it only through processed in-game use after the owner clears it; `CYRUS_SOUND_LIBRARY_CLEARED` stays off, so custome

## Minecraft reference and bring-your-own game assets (policy)
The owner supplied Minecraft game archives. They are **game-derived reference, private**. Rules: never in the community library, never served to customers, never in git, never summarised in these docs. Built in r42 (`feature/cyrus-r42-mcref`, NOT deployed, every switch off):

